# The pre-registration of TraderSpider's forecast lines (V7.2 Stage 3, 17 October 2026): append-only. A registration line says what will be judged, on what, by which line and under which engine version, before the figure; a result line answers it with the figure, its interval, the verdict and the commit, and carries the hash of its registration's locked fields (shared/forecast/preregistration.ts; tests/preregistration.test.ts refuses an edited registration). Stages 1 and 2 were measured before this file existed: their lines are the V7.2 plan's, entered with the engine version they were measured under.
{"line":"registration","id":"V72-S1-INTERVALS","registeredAt":"2026-10-17T00:30:00Z","engineVersion":"8ccc65988f1f","hypothesis":"A circular block bootstrap over the record's hours, in blocks as long as the horizon, with a dependence correction for overlapping outcomes and Student's t for few blocks, gives every figure a valid 95% interval.","metric":"The share of simulated panels (10 pairs, a market factor and each pair's own noise, moving sums over the horizon, true 80% coverage 0.8) whose 95% interval holds the truth, a thousand panels a horizon.","successLine":"93-97% at every horizon, for the 80% and the 50% coverage.","judgedOn":"simulated panels, tests/forecastUncertainty.test.ts","kind":"confirmatory","constants":["forecast.uncertainty"]}
{"line":"registration","id":"V72-S1-NODIRECTION","registeredAt":"2026-10-17T00:30:00Z","engineVersion":"8ccc65988f1f","hypothesis":"On the record of 16 October no direction model has a skill its sample can tell from zero.","metric":"Each direction source's Brier skill over the better of an even chance and the base rate, with its 95% interval, per horizon.","successLine":"No interval excludes zero on the positive side at any horizon (a prediction, not a goal).","judgedOn":"run-20261016-0640, the lab12h profile","kind":"confirmatory"}
{"line":"registration","id":"V72-S2-DIRECTIONBAR","registeredAt":"2026-10-17T01:30:00Z","engineVersion":"704b82f0f396","hypothesis":"A direction checklist asking a skill of 1%, 200 calls whose precision's lower bound clears an even chance, a skill above zero in both halves of the weeks and of the pairs, no class under -1% on 2,000 outcomes and -- for tradeable -- the calls' edge after the round trip above zero beyond noise promotes nothing under 1% skill and almost never promotes noise.","metric":"The model-horizons promoted on the real record; the false-pass rate per model-horizon under 200 day shifts of the outcomes (each hour's cross-section intact).","successLine":"Nothing under 1% skill promoted; a false-pass rate of at most 5% per model-horizon, against V7.1's 3-26%.","judgedOn":"run-20261016-0640, research/directionNull.ts","kind":"confirmatory","constants":["forecast.directionModels.promotion"]}
{"line":"registration","id":"V72-S2-EXPLORATORY","registeredAt":"2026-10-17T01:30:00Z","engineVersion":"704b82f0f396","hypothesis":"The distribution's skew, its median in half-widths, the excursion asymmetry and the shorter horizons' agreement carry no direction the checklist would promote.","metric":"Each reading mapped by the weeks before and judged by the direction bar in cells by market state, regime and class; the passes against the cells tried.","successLine":"Any pass is recorded as a null until it repeats on the next walk forward; the passes are weighed against the false-pass rate times the cells tried.","judgedOn":"run-20261016-0640, research/directionNull.ts","kind":"exploratory"}
{"line":"registration","id":"V72-S3-LOCK","registeredAt":"2026-10-17T03:00:00Z","engineVersion":"704b82f0f396","hypothesis":"A registry whose results carry the hash of their registration's locked fields refuses an edited registration, a duplicate id and a result without a registration; every engine constant added since 16 October 2026 is named by a registration or is infrastructure.","metric":"tests/preregistration.test.ts on the real file and on tampered copies.","successLine":"Every tampered copy refused; the real file clean; every constant added since 16 October 2026 named.","judgedOn":"research/preregistered.jsonl","kind":"confirmatory"}
{"line":"registration","id":"V72-S3-CHALLENGER","registeredAt":"2026-10-17T03:00:00Z","engineVersion":"704b82f0f396","hypothesis":"Two walk forwards a day apart differ by noise: paired on the hours both tested, a nightly refit's pinball, coverage and direction-skill differences hold zero at every horizon, and a challenger judged beyond noise adopts no refit that is within noise and under a week newer.","metric":"The paired 90% intervals of the differences per horizon on the two-day run's refit pair (run-20261017-0030 against run-20261016-1236) and on later refits; adoptions per week and the count of adopted refits whose intervals held zero everywhere.","successLine":"The two-day run's pair reads within noise at every horizon; zero adoptions of a refit within noise and under seven days newer.","judgedOn":"the multiday2 profile's runs; research/pairedChallenge.ts","kind":"confirmatory","constants":["forecast.challenger.newerDays","forecast.challenger.level"]}
{"line":"registration","id":"V72-S4-CLOCK","registeredAt":"2026-10-17T03:00:00Z","engineVersion":"704b82f0f396","hypothesis":"The clock is already learned: no band of the UTC day has the forecast's 80% range hold far from 80%.","metric":"The cross-fitted 80% coverage by UTC hour (24 buckets) per horizon, in four halves (two pair halves by week 1-2 against week 3), n per cell, PRE_EVENT rows out.","successLine":"An hour band fails only under 70% or over 90% in all four halves with n >= 500 each; no failing band at any horizon means Stage 9 carries no CLOCK block.","judgedOn":"run-20261016-0640 and the two-day run's record; research/byHour.ts","kind":"confirmatory"}
{"line":"registration","id":"V72-S4-ABLATION","registeredAt":"2026-10-17T03:00:00Z","engineVersion":"704b82f0f396","hypothesis":"The walk forward is deterministic by seed and a feature block's worth can be read as a paired difference on identical folds.","metric":"Two fits with every block read, row by row; a fit with a block permuted across the tested weeks against the full fit.","successLine":"Two full fits differ by zero at every row; the permuted control's pinball difference is under 0.2% in absolute value.","judgedOn":"a scratch profile's bars; research/ablation.ts","kind":"confirmatory"}
{"line":"registration","id":"V72-S5-FIDELITY","registeredAt":"2026-10-17T03:00:00Z","engineVersion":"704b82f0f396","hypothesis":"The forecast pass as pure functions replays a recorded run.","metric":"The share of the 12-hour run's grid forecasts that replay to four decimals on V2's own levels, every remainder listed with its reason.","successLine":"At least 99% replay to four decimals; the gate green; the tape's lines counted on the next run's report.","judgedOn":"the lab12h profile's record","kind":"confirmatory"}
{"line":"registration","id":"V72-S6-REPLAY","registeredAt":"2026-10-17T03:00:00Z","engineVersion":"704b82f0f396","hypothesis":"The tested weeks can be replayed out of sample at every five-minute close through the live decision, deterministically and fast.","metric":"Two replays compared byte by byte; the time to replay 90 days; the four strategies' out-of-sample trades, net after 0.24%, profit factor and interval.","successLine":"Two replays byte-identical; 90 days under 15 minutes on this machine; the strategies' figures reported with intervals (the expectation: few trades).","judgedOn":"the lab12h and multiday2 profiles' bars and fold models","kind":"confirmatory"}
{"line":"registration","id":"V72-S7-ARCHIVE","registeredAt":"2026-10-17T03:00:00Z","engineVersion":"704b82f0f396","hypothesis":"A year of five-minute bars can be fetched from the public archive, checked against its published checksums, with the universe chosen per month from the archive itself.","metric":"Checksums matched per month; the per-month universe with the pairs that entered and left; the fetch resumable.","successLine":"Every month's checksum matches; the universe listed per month; no claim about the market.","judgedOn":"data.binance.vision monthly klines into a scratch profile's forecastArchive/","kind":"confirmatory"}
{"line":"registration","id":"V72-S8-WINDOW","registeredAt":"2026-10-17T03:00:00Z","engineVersion":"704b82f0f396","hypothesis":"Expanding training beats rolling on the long walk forward, or does not.","metric":"Pooled honest pinball per mode at every horizon over twelve tested weeks, coverage80 pooled and per week, with intervals.","successLine":"Expanding beats rolling on pinball by at least 1% at three of five horizons with coverage within 2 points of 80% everywhere; the reverse is the recorded result.","judgedOn":"the year of archive bars; research/longWalkForward.ts","kind":"confirmatory"}
{"line":"registration","id":"V72-S8-DIRECTION","registeredAt":"2026-10-17T03:00:00Z","engineVersion":"704b82f0f396","hypothesis":"On a year of bars no horizon has direction on these features.","metric":"Each direction source's skill over the year with hour-block intervals and the sign per month.","successLine":"A horizon has direction only if its skill interval excludes zero over the year and the sign holds in at least 70% of months; otherwise no direction at these horizons on these features is the settled finding.","judgedOn":"the year of archive bars; research/longWalkForward.ts","kind":"confirmatory"}
{"line":"registration","id":"V72-S8-COVERAGE","registeredAt":"2026-10-17T03:00:00Z","engineVersion":"704b82f0f396","hypothesis":"The calibration procedure holds 80% over a year, week by week.","metric":"coverage80 pooled and per tested week at every horizon over twelve weeks.","successLine":"Within 80 +/- 2 pooled and within +/- 5 in at least 80% of tested weeks at every horizon; otherwise the procedure, not the market, is the problem.","judgedOn":"the year of archive bars; research/longWalkForward.ts","kind":"confirmatory"}
{"line":"registration","id":"V72-S8-CADENCE","registeredAt":"2026-10-17T03:00:00Z","engineVersion":"704b82f0f396","hypothesis":"A day of new rows changes a fit within noise.","metric":"Fits at day D and D+1, D+7, D+28 with the same seeds scored on the same later weeks, paired by hour.","successLine":"If the D+1 paired difference's interval holds zero at every horizon on at least 80% of start days, a weekly refit with a nightly recalibration is designed (a product change only with the user's yes); otherwise nightly stays.","judgedOn":"the year of archive bars; research/longWalkForward.ts","kind":"confirmatory"}
{"line":"registration","id":"V72-S9-CROSS","registeredAt":"2026-10-17T03:00:00Z","engineVersion":"704b82f0f396","hypothesis":"Cross-sectional and taker-size features add direction at the short horizons.","metric":"The ablation of the CROSS and FLOW blocks against v2 on identical folds: each direction model's honest skill, calls and precision under the direction bar; the btc_gap_15m decile table per tested week.","successLine":"A direction model's honest skill at least +1% at five or fifteen minutes on at least 5,000 outcomes, its precision at 0.58 not below the baseline's, the decile table monotone the same way in every tested week; a win is a truer P(up), never a trade.","judgedOn":"the walk forward with features-v3 blocks; research/ablation.ts, research/crossSection.ts","kind":"confirmatory"}
{"line":"registration","id":"V72-S9-CLOCK","registeredAt":"2026-10-17T03:00:00Z","engineVersion":"704b82f0f396","hypothesis":"Where Stage 4 found a failing band, a diurnal scale of the usual move lowers the pinball loss.","metric":"The ablation of the CLOCK block: pooled honest pinball, the by-hour coverage range, pooled coverage, the ACI steps' size.","successLine":"Pooled honest pinball lower by at least 0.5% at five minutes, fifteen or an hour with the paired interval excluding zero, the by-hour coverage range at least halved, pooled coverage within 2 points of 80%, the ACI steps not larger.","judgedOn":"the walk forward with the CLOCK block; research/ablation.ts","kind":"confirmatory"}
{"line":"registration","id":"V72-S10-POSITIONING","registeredAt":"2026-10-17T03:00:00Z","engineVersion":"704b82f0f396","hypothesis":"Futures positioning (funding, premium, open interest and taker changes, never levels) sharpens the four-hour and day ranges or their direction.","metric":"The ablation of the POSITIONING block at four hours and a day: paired pinball with its interval, coverage pooled and by state, each direction model's skill, calls and precision under the direction bar, the week-permuted control.","successLine":"Pooled honest pinball at least 1.0% lower on identical rows with the paired 95% interval excluding zero and coverage within 2 points of 80%, and/or a direction model's skill at least +1% at four hours or a day on at least 5,000 outcomes with the sign positive in every tested week; the permuted control under 0.2%.","judgedOn":"the walk forward with the POSITIONING block; research/positioningForecast.ts","kind":"confirmatory"}
{"line":"registration","id":"V72-S11-BAND","registeredAt":"2026-10-17T03:00:00Z","engineVersion":"704b82f0f396","hypothesis":"A resting bid at the cross-fitted P10 with an exit at the median earns after costs without a call; the expectation at four hours and under is a kill, the one cell with a positive prior RECOVERY after a down-shock at one to four hours.","metric":"Fill share, net per fill after costs, profit factor, the excess over the same hold from arbitrary closes, t on hourly means, by horizon and by the market state at the fill; the share of net from the best 5% of hours; the median time to exit.","successLine":"Net per fill above zero after costs and an excess over the usual of at least +0.10% with t >= 2 on both pair halves, at least 200 fills a half, no more than half the net from the best 5% of hours; a pass must repeat on the replay of Stage 6 before anything is built on it.","judgedOn":"the walk forward's bars; research/bandReversion.ts","kind":"confirmatory"}
{"line":"registration","id":"V72-S12-WINDOW","registeredAt":"2026-10-17T03:00:00Z","engineVersion":"704b82f0f396","hypothesis":"A conditions verdict (OPEN, CAUTION, CLOSED) from the states, the drift gate, UNCERTAIN width, the spread shock and the volatility ratio marks the moments a forecast should not be acted on.","metric":"The lab strategies' and the forecast trader's trades by the verdict at entry on the replay and the live record: net after costs, profit factor, with intervals.","successLine":"Trades entered under CLOSED net less after costs than under OPEN with the interval excluding zero on the replay; the verdict ships shown and off.","judgedOn":"the replay of Stage 6 and the next multi-day run","kind":"confirmatory"}
{"line":"registration","id":"V72-S13-BUNDLE","registeredAt":"2026-10-17T03:00:00Z","engineVersion":"704b82f0f396","hypothesis":"One evaluation bundle makes every table of the report from a profile, each figure with its interval.","metric":"The bundle's tables against the one-off readers' on the same profile.","successLine":"Every table of research/FORECAST.md's V7.2 sections is made by the bundle, each figure with its interval and its registration id; the one-off readers retired.","judgedOn":"the lab12h and multiday2 profiles","kind":"confirmatory"}
